chapter(3,'english','paper-boats','Paper Boats',
 ('A stream, a boat and a naughty boy','Meena floats paper boats on a stream near a bamboo bridge. A boy keeps overturning them, and Meena gets angry. But when the boy says he does not know how to make a boat, Meena chooses to teach him instead of fighting. In this chapter you will read this story, learn new words, use he and she in place of names, and use the little words in, on and under to tell where things are.'),
 [('Meet the story',['The story takes place near a stream with a bamboo bridge.','Meena puts a paper boat into the water and it sails swiftly down the stream, and she is delighted.','She goes on putting several boats into the stream, one after another.','Then she sees a naughty boy pushing and overturning the boats.']),
  ('The quarrel and how it ends',['Meena stares at the boy angrily and shouts Stop, but he does not stop.','When she asks why, he says it is fun for him, and Meena replies that the boats are hers and he must stop.','The boy thinks for a minute and promises not to do it again, but he says he also wants to play.','He admits that he does not know how to fold paper into a boat.','Meena does not run to complain. She shows him how to fold and re-fold the coloured paper.','Soon both of them have boats on the stream, and both enjoy watching them sail.','This tells us that helping someone is a better answer to a problem than staying angry.']),
  ('New words',['Delighted means very happy. Meena was delighted when her boat sailed fast.','Several means more than two but not very many. Meena made several boats.','Overturning means turning something upside down, so the boat floats badly or sinks.','A stream is a small narrow river. Watched means looked at carefully for some time.']),
  ('Using he and she',['We do not need to say a name again and again. We can use a small word in its place.','For a girl or a woman we use she. Instead of saying Meena walked and Meena bent, we say Meena walked and she bent.','For a boy or a man we use he. Instead of saying the boy jumped and the boy pulled, we say the boy jumped and he pulled.','So Rani likes playing outside and she likes flying kites. Sahil has a top and he plays with it every day.']),
  ('In, on and under',['Some small words tell us where a thing is. They are called prepositions.','On means resting on top of something, like a book on the shelf.','In means inside something, like books in a bag or a ball in a box.','Under means below something, like a ball under the table.','To choose the right word, look at the picture and ask where the thing really is.']),
  ('Speak, write and play',['In Let us speak, you tell the story of Manish saves the ant from the pictures, in order, beginning with what happened first.','In Let us write, you look at a park picture and write a few sentences using clues like children, playing, see-saw, swings, slide, enjoying and happy.','The crossword has answers about toys and games, such as top, bat, ball, marble and swing.','At home you can ask your elders which games they played when they were young and learn one to share with friends.']),
 ],
 [('Fill in he or she: Durga is five years old. ___ is going to school.',[('Durga is a girl, so we use she.','He is for a boy, she is for a girl.'),('The sentence becomes: She is going to school.','She takes the place of Durga.')]),
  ('Choose in, on or under: The bag is ___ the chair (the bag is sitting on top of the chair).',[('Look at where the bag is: on the seat of the chair.','On means resting on top.'),('So we write: The bag is on the chair.','In would mean inside, and under would mean below.')]),
  ('Put the story events in order: A. They both sail their boats. B. Meena shows him how to fold paper. C. The boy overturns the boats.',[('First the boy overturns the boats.','That is the problem.'),('Next Meena shows him how to fold paper.','That is the solution.'),('At the end they both sail boats. The order is C, B, A.','Stories have a beginning, a middle and an end.')])],
 ('Tell the story of Meena and the boy in your own words, and say what it teaches.',['Meena put paper boats in a stream','A boy overturned them','Meena taught him to make boats','Helping is better than staying angry'],['Meena ran home to complain','The boy ran away','Meena had only white paper']),
 ['Meena helped the boy by teaching him to fold paper boats.','Delighted means very happy; several means more than two.','He is used for a boy and she is used for a girl.','On means on top, in means inside, under means below.','Kindness can turn a quarrel into play.'],
 [M('1',1,'What was Meena playing with?','Paper boats',[('Kites','The story is about boats on a stream'),('A top','Meena put boats in the stream')],'Meena was floating paper boats on the stream.'),
  M('2',1,'Why was Meena angry?','The boy was overturning her boats',[('The boy took her paper','He did not take paper, he overturned the boats'),('The stream was dry','The stream had water')],'She was angry because the boy kept pushing her boats over.'),
  M('3',1,'How did Meena help the boy?','She showed him how to make paper boats',[('She gave him a toy','She taught him instead'),('She sent him away','She helped him')],'She taught him to fold and re-fold the paper.'),
  F('4',1,'The boy thought it was fun to overturn paper boats.',True,'He said it was fun.'),
  F('5',1,'Meena ran home to complain about the boy.',False,'She stayed and helped him instead.'),
  F('6',1,'Meena had only white paper.',False,'She had coloured paper of different sizes.'),
  M('7',2,'What does delighted mean?','Very happy',[('Very angry','That is the opposite'),('Very tired','Not the meaning')],'Meena was happy when the boat sailed.'),
  M('8',2,'Which word fits: Sahil has a top. ___ plays with it every day.','He',[('She','Sahil is a boy'),('It','It is not used for a boy')],'Sahil is a boy, so he is used.'),
  M('9',2,'Which word fits: The ball is ___ the box (inside it).','in',[('on','On means on top'),('under','Under means below')],'Inside the box means in.'),
  M('10',2,'Which word fits: The car is ___ the table (below it).','under',[('on','On would mean on top'),('in','In would mean inside')],'Below the table means under.'),
  S('11',2,'What word do we use in place of Rani, a girl?',['she'],'We use she for a girl.',wrong=[('he','He is for a boy')]),
  M('12',3,'What does the story teach us?','Helping is better than staying angry',[('Never share paper','Meena shared and both were happy'),('Never play near a stream','The story is about sharing and helping')],'Meena helped the boy and both enjoyed the game.')],
 svgs=[('c3en-paper-boats-prepositions','Three pictures show a ball on a table, in a box and under a table.','On, in and under tell us where a thing is.')],
 keep=['stream','delighted'])
